  "limitations": [
    "Complete original exterior reconstructed from three inspected ordinary complex/tower photographs,exact retained OSM/Q845846 complex outline and standard viewer PMTiles/global terrain. No downloaded mesh,private photo texture,bespoke survey or archive research. Interiors,furnished rooms,individual signs/artwork,exact original equipment inventory and surrounding city are excluded.",
    "The current standard map establishes the whole365.477x200.622m casino complex,75m bent hotel slab,350m circular tower projection and rooftop swimming-pool outline. Tower centerX15.5,Z73.75 and the asymmetrical hotel/court/strip relationship sign the NNE/SSW frame. Adjacent25m northwestern parking garage remains native map content. Casino14m and lower pool-wing24m heights,24 reconstructed hotel rows,pane counts,pod/buttress levels and profiles,entry drum and roof plant are photographic approximations. Overall map heights are generalized,not surveyed schedules.",
    "Tower has three real tapering buttresses,open lower and upper gaps,central shaft,circular glass entrance drum,separate lattice lower cone and sloping glass observation pod,terraces/roof and red-white lattice mast with thin tip reaching350m. Primary venue Big Shot page gives a921ft platform,used as approximate281m mast base;pod levels are photographic reconstructions. Static simplified carriage/seat forms suggest the mast platform;no ride motion,safety/operations claim or exact ride-equipment replica. Historical external green thrill-ride arms in older photos are not copied.",
    "Detailed source retains individual hotel panes/recess returns,projecting floor bands,mullions,pod lattice,railings,denser mast braces and original schematic roof plant. Four browser tiers preserve the whole resort and tower. Far tiers aggregate roof plant,rails,mast braces and glazing;skyline uses fewer leg/pod facets. Existing shared256px concrete,window grid,painted metal,roof membrane and granite graphs plus palette pool water use no private or embedded images. Glazing/water are stylized opaque surfaces,not optical interiors or a pool simulation.",
    "Unmodified129x129/4m field oversamples two standard global DEM tiles. Base reference622m is rounded from the tower-center sample;podium skirts,individual leg feet and entrance drum embed below that field. Exact curb/foundation/roof-pool depths,accessible gradients,original steps and terrain grades remain unsurveyed. Estimated tier errors8/4/2/1m are not certified mesh distances. Physical phone/laptop and dense-city timing remain unmeasured."
